      "documentConcept": "Salesforce Case change events and severity-transition qualification",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:2c889596e46d520b6ad0a7cc0809301f76d32065894c733e9dda3aad87e71d49",
      "text": "Case change events provide record-change input for alert qualification. Native CDC omits prior values, so a specific old-to-new severity transition needs retained state or suitable field history. Pub/Sub consumers must decode field-change bitmaps and distinguish unchanged empty values from fields actually nulled. Value filters and enrichment do not establish that severity changed. Transaction consolidation also means a Case created and reprioritized before commit can arrive as a creation with its final priority. The alert specification must define its severity field, target values, required prior state, and treatment of creation.",
      "sources": [
        "https://architect.salesforce.com/docs/architect/decision-guides/guide/record-triggered",
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-enrich-considerations.html",
